=== reading ===
  The professional book stands ~$800K within 5c per covered game
  at 1c spreads; niche games get 1/100th of that (~$6K) and stay
  CALIBRATED; headline outrights carry real depth (~$235K median
  among top-volume fields) and are MISCALIBRATED anyway, while
  74% of the outright tail has no two-sided book at all. Standing
  liquidity neither rescues one-shot markets nor is needed by
  repeated ones — reinforcing repetition, not liquidity, as the
  active ingredient. The fee menu points the same way: makers
  PAY fees where they queue to quote (covered games) and make
  free where the exchange needs them (niche, outrights, politics).
